WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.344
AI can produce a working app before its builder
understands the system.

00:00:05.344 --> 00:00:12.470
Even a one-line change can send a beginner back to an
assistant to reread the repository.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.697
GroundTruth addresses that next-change moment.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:23.454
The goal is a builder who understands the code and
architecture, then practises making a change
independently.

00:00:23.454 --> 00:00:29.537
This edited walkthrough uses real hosted interface
captures and a synthetic demonstration account.

00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:35.064
Bring a public GitHub repository and choose a feature to
strengthen.

00:00:35.064 --> 00:00:39.364
Our small study-task project makes the journey easy to
inspect.

00:00:39.364 --> 00:00:46.245
The learner chooses a backend workflow, rather than
needing to know which file to open first.

00:00:47.083 --> 00:00:56.621
GroundTruth explains the selected workflow with a beginner
overview, reading flow, glossary and visible source at a
pinned commit.

00:00:56.621 --> 00:00:59.131
Where does the request go?

00:00:59.131 --> 00:01:01.139
Which component validates it?

00:01:01.139 --> 00:01:05.155
The learner connects individual lines to system
responsibilities.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.870
A small concept tree links the workflow to focused
practice.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:14.765
The learner can strengthen validation before moving on.

00:01:14.765 --> 00:01:22.556
Muse Spark generates contextual learning content from the
selected source and goal, within a consistent interface.

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:29.553
A beginner can start with an MCQ, then try a tiny coding
task.

00:01:29.553 --> 00:01:32.423
Questions belong to this selected code.

00:01:32.423 --> 00:01:37.208
The model's suggested answer is still reviewable against
the source.

00:01:37.208 --> 00:01:41.035
A generated explanation is not automatically a fact.

00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:44.913
The independent attempt changes the rules.

00:01:44.913 --> 00:01:49.019
New study assistance pauses while the learner answers.

00:01:49.019 --> 00:01:53.125
The first submitted response is retained before feedback.

00:01:53.125 --> 00:01:59.285
The learner can also end an attempt without inventing a
completed answer.

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:02.364
Outside tools remain beyond GroundTruth's control.

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:07.162
Progress brings the attempt and observed app activity
together.

00:02:07.162 --> 00:02:14.265
The concept index is provisional evidence, not an
automatic grade or a validated measure of mastery.

00:02:14.265 --> 00:02:19.148
The learner decides which project to share with an
approved teacher.

00:02:19.917 --> 00:02:24.713
The teacher reviews the original attempt and relevant
activity.

00:02:24.713 --> 00:02:28.976
Class enrollment alone does not expose every project.

00:02:28.976 --> 00:02:35.903
A working AI-built application starts the conversation;
the learner's independent attempt adds evidence.

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:38.794
Meta supplies contextual guidance.

00:02:38.794 --> 00:02:45.708
GroundTruth on Vercel controls access and learning state,
with Supabase preserving the evidence.

00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:54.218
Our aim is simple: understand the code, think in systems,
and make the next change yourself.
